 11 │ theorem allTwo ∀ (b: Bool) (c: Bool): List.all [b, c] (x => x) = b := ?
    │                                                                       ┬  
    │                                                                       ╰── b: Bool
    │                                                                           c: Bool
    │                                                                           ⊢ [b, c].all (x => x) = b
    │                                                                             computes to (b && c && True) = b
    │ 
    │ Note: this statement is false; a counterexample:
    │         b = True
    │         c = False
    │       `[b, c].all (x => x) = b` is false:
    │         left:  False
    │         right: True
